WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:11.500
60. Greek Theater and Dionysus. Hollywood blockbusters, musicals, one-man plays, in

2
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:18.080
fact the entire tradition of Western theater, can be traced back to one Greek god. Dionysus

3
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:24.880
was the god of wine and fertility. His followers would drink, dance, and become wild, moving

4
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:30.480
and singing as though they had lost control. Dionysus was supposed to be worshipped by

5
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:37.060
satyrs, mythical creatures that were part goat, part man. During festivals, the human

6
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:43.940
followers of Dionysus would dress up as these satyrs. They would sing and dance as a chorus,

7
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:49.580
telling stories about their god. This ensemble was always performed as a group until one

8
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:57.740
day about 2,500 years ago when one person stepped forward to speak lines on his own.

9
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:03.720
It may have been a priest called Thespis. Whoever it was, he told a story in words rather

10
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:10.760
than song. He was the first actor. Theater became popular after that. It evolved into

11
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:18.760
three types, tragedy, comedy, and satyr plays. Originally Greek theater had three very distinct

12
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:25.360
parts. It would start with a prologue or speech about the play, then the chorus would enter,

13
00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.900
and then the scenes of the play would be performed. At first, only a few actors were allowed on

14
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:37.660
stage at one time. The chorus was very important for giving information to the audience. These

15
00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:43.500
new performances needed space. One of the first spaces was the theater of Dionysus in

16
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:50.580
Athens. It was built into a slope of a hill. The stage was set below the seats on the hillside

17
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:57.360
where 25,000 people could sit and hear all the action happening. Theaters and acting

18
00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:03.320
evolved from that point, eventually becoming the variety of styles we have today. Next

19
00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:09.600
time you watch things blow up at the cinema, remember Dionysus and his wild worshippers,

20
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.840
and maybe whisper a quick thank you.
